From: sbc-builder <root@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: RTL8211F: disable ALDPS when the MAC needs RXC

ALDPS (link-down power saving) stops the RTL8211F's RXC clock while there is
no link. rtl8211f_config_aldps() only ever sets ALDPS (DT opt-in) and keeps
whatever the PHY had otherwise - which after a hardware reset can be ALDPS
on. stmmac asks for RXC to stay on (mac_requires_rxc ->
PHY_F_RXC_ALWAYS_ON) because its DMA software reset cannot complete without
it; on RK3566 boards (Radxa ZERO 3E) the first open before link-up then fails
with "Failed to reset the dma". Clear ALDPS when that flag is set.

---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -751,9 +751,17 @@
 		   RTL8211F_ALDPS_ENABLE |
 		   RTL8211F_ALDPS_XTAL_OFF;
 
-	/* The value is preserved if the device tree property is absent */
-	if (!priv->enable_aldps)
+	if (!priv->enable_aldps) {
+		/* The MAC needs RXC (e.g. stmmac cannot finish its DMA reset
+		 * without it): make sure ALDPS is off, whatever the PHY's reset
+		 * default or the bootloader left behind.
+		 */
+		if (phydev->dev_flags & PHY_F_RXC_ALWAYS_ON)
+			return phy_modify(phydev, RTL8211F_PHYCR1, mask, 0);
+
+		/* Otherwise the value is preserved */
 		return 0;
+	}
 
 	return phy_modify(phydev, RTL8211F_PHYCR1, mask, mask);
 }
